  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2314216386f93e848b802d3e5aa8e609, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tetanus
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MedicalCase
  title: Generalized Tetanus
  type: Uncommon / Emergency
  category: Infectious - Bacterial
  description: A vaccine-preventable disease that remains endemic in the Philippines,
    carrying a high mortality rate (29% in local tertiary studies).
  symptoms: 'Trismus (lockjaw) and difficulty swallowing.   Back pain and muscle
    rigidity.   Risus sardonicus (frozen grin) and muscle spasms triggered by minor
    stimuli. '
  pathology: Caused by the tetanospasmin toxin blocking inhibitory signals. The bacteria
    typically enters through puncture wounds (like stepping on a rusty nail) with
    an incubation period of 5-10 days.
  treatment: Immediate ICU hospitalization and administration of Tetanus Immune Globulin
    (TIG).   Wound debridement, antibiotics, and muscle relaxants.   Respiratory
    support if distress occurs.
  keyFeatures: A rusty nail injury followed by trismus is considered tetanus until
    proven otherwise.
  requiredStageLevel: 1
